# [CHANGE: claude-code | 2026-08-27]
# Single front door for the media server. See DECISION 84.
#
# Why a proxy at all: before this, every app was its own bare-HTTP port and you had to
# remember seven of them. Now there is one name to remember, everything is encrypted,
# and the landing page links to the rest.
#
# THREE addresses reach the same thing, and the difference between them matters:
#   luminos-server.tail1fd435.ts.net   real Let's Encrypt cert, no browser warning
#   100.82.125.26                      same box over Tailscale, by IP, local CA
#   192.168.2.61                       at home on the LAN, local CA
#
# WHY THE NAME AND THE IPs ARE IN SEPARATE BLOCKS. A certificate is issued for a NAME.
# Let's Encrypt will not put a private IP in one, so the two IP addresses can only ever
# use Caddy's local CA and will always show a browser warning. Prefer the name.
#
# WHY `tls <files>` AND NOT `tls { get_certificate tailscale }`. Caddy can fetch these
# itself, but tailscaled refuses cert requests from a non-root process unless that user
# is made the tailnet OPERATOR -- and an operator can run `tailscale down`. Handing that
# to an internet-facing web server would turn a Caddy compromise into a Tailscale
# compromise. Instead `luminos-tailscale-cert.timer` fetches as root once a day and
# drops the files here, group-readable by caddy only. The cost of that choice is that
# renewal is a timer's job now; the unit fails loudly at 30 days left so a broken timer
# surfaces in `systemctl list-units --failed` rather than as a dead site in three months.
#
# WHAT THIS DOES NOT DO: it does not add authentication. Every app behind it was tested
# first and each one demands a login even when the request arrives from 127.0.0.1 --
# which is what every request looks like once it comes through here. That test is the
# whole point: Radarr/Sonarr/Prowlarr used to be "DisabledForLocalAddresses", and a
# proxy in front of that setting would have silently deleted the login prompt for
# everybody. They were switched to "Enabled" first, on 2026-08-27, and re-tested through
# this proxy afterwards. If you add an app here, hit it from 127.0.0.1 with no
# credentials FIRST and confirm you are refused.
#
# ONE PORT PER APP, not sub-paths. Sub-paths were tried and abandoned:
# Radarr/Sonarr/Prowlarr have a urlBase setting, but it only rewrites the UI shell --
# their login page stays at /login and their API stays at /api/ no matter what it is set
# to, so three apps under one name all fight over /login. Jellyfin, Jellyseerr and
# luminos-space have no base-path setting at all. Jellyfin is additionally left
# untouched on purpose: giving it a base URL would break the Roku's saved server
# address, and the TV working matters more than tidy URLs.

{
	# Never talk to a public CA from here. The only real certificate on this box is the
	# tailnet one, and tailscaled obtains that -- not Caddy. Without this, Caddy tries
	# Let's Encrypt for names and IPs that have no public DNS record, fails NXDOMAIN
	# forever, and the visible symptom is a TLS handshake that HANGS for 20+ seconds
	# rather than any error message.
	local_certs
}

(proxy) {
	# {args[0]} is the loopback port of the app being fronted.
	header {
		-Server
		X-Content-Type-Options "nosniff"
		Referrer-Policy "no-referrer"
	}
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:{args[0]}
}

(tsname) {
	tls /var/lib/luminos/tls/cert.pem /var/lib/luminos/tls/key.pem
}

# --- the landing page :443 ----------------------------------------------------
luminos-server.tail1fd435.ts.net {
	import tsname
	import proxy 8100
}
100.82.125.26, 192.168.2.61 {
	tls internal
	import proxy 8100
}

# --- Jellyfin :8443 -----------------------------------------------------------
luminos-server.tail1fd435.ts.net:8443 {
	import tsname
	import proxy 8096
}
100.82.125.26:8443, 192.168.2.61:8443 {
	tls internal
	import proxy 8096
}

# --- Jellyseerr :8444 ---------------------------------------------------------
luminos-server.tail1fd435.ts.net:8444 {
	import tsname
	import proxy 5055
}
100.82.125.26:8444, 192.168.2.61:8444 {
	tls internal
	import proxy 5055
}

# --- NZBGet :8445 -------------------------------------------------------------
luminos-server.tail1fd435.ts.net:8445 {
	import tsname
	import proxy 6789
}
100.82.125.26:8445, 192.168.2.61:8445 {
	tls internal
	import proxy 6789
}

# --- luminos-space :8446 ------------------------------------------------------
# Its page reads the token out of the query string in JavaScript, so the token has to
# be in the URL. Putting it here means the hub tile is a plain link and the token never
# has to be typed or remembered.
(spacetoken) {
	@needtoken {
		path /
		not query token=*
	}
	redir @needtoken /?token=REDACTED_SEE_mobile-setup.txt
}
luminos-server.tail1fd435.ts.net:8446 {
	import tsname
	import spacetoken
	import proxy 8099
}
100.82.125.26:8446, 192.168.2.61:8446 {
	tls internal
	import spacetoken
	import proxy 8099
}

